#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Assign a right-scoped, non-compute-heavy item from the parent Swarm Work Item's idle-backlog queue (documentation, metadata, review checklists, or disjoint lightweight edits in a separate git worktree, never running git checkout inside the active build's worktree) instead of letting the worker sleep on passive timers."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:83
#. Diagram label
msgid "Assign non-heavy idle backlog"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:141
#. Diagram label
msgid "Cold-start handover runbook"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Executes one stall-safe Swarm Monitor check-in sweep inside Process_SwarmDispatchAndMonitor: extracts live worker progress, measures repository queues and host CPU, disk, and compressed or swapped memory, intervenes on leaks or stalls, assigns right-scoped non-heavy idle-backlog work to workers waiting on single-core compute without checking out mid-build, refreshes and pushes the parent Swarm Work Item's Cold-Start Handover Runbook to the shared beans store on every sweep, and publishes the standardized two-table Human-Consumable Swarm Status Report when requested on-demand or scheduled periodically."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Immediately SIGKILL any runaway subprocess leaking into compressed memory or swapfiles and message its worker; nudge a silent worker via SendMessage; route dead sessions through stalled-agent-triage; or pull the Andon cord to halt remaining workers on structural divergence or host exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:129
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Join after optional human status report emission to return control to Process_SwarmDispatchAndMonitor."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Join after optional stall or swap-leak intervention before checking whether any worker is idle on single-core compute."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Join before refreshing the parent Swarm Work Item's Cold-Start Handover Runbook."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:41
#. Diagram label
msgid "Monitor wakeup or check-in"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:147
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nudge, kill leak or pull Andon"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "On every routine monitor check-in tick and milestone transition (whether chat reporting is periodic or quiet on-demand), update the parent Swarm Work Item's Cold-Start Handover Runbook (origin/main SHA, EC-1..EC-k exit status, merged/open PR wave queues, worktree-to-branch-to-HEAD-to-role/PID table, verbatim owner directives and safety fences, and under-60-second cold-takeover commands plus dispatch lines) and push immediately to cat/cat-harness/beans via swarm-epic-sync / state:push."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:136
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Progress, headroom, idle-backlog assignments, Cold-Start Handover Runbook in beans, and any due human status report are complete for this check-in."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:121
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish scoreboard and status table"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:122
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Publish the standardized two-table Human-Consumable Swarm Status Report with zero naked worker codes, bare PR ranges, or unglossed bean IDs: (Table 1) Live Repository Queue Scoreboard across PRs, Work Items, and Issues with host headroom, and (Table 2) Full Multi-Track End-State, Queue, and Worker Status Table stating EC-1..EC-k progress and plain-English proved or measured outcomes."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:156
#. Diagram label
msgid "Quiet"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Refresh and push epic handover"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:113
#. Diagram label
msgid "Report requested or periodic?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run the targeted JSONL progress extractor, query live forge PR/issue counts and synced beans states against origin/main, and inspect CPU load, root disk free space (df -h /), and total plus compressed/swap memory (top -l 1 -o mem -stats pid,command,mem,cmprs on macOS or VmRSS + VmSwap on Linux, never ps -o rss alone)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor-sweep.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs every monitor wake (event-driven completion, routine check-in tick, or on-demand owner request): checks worker progress and compressed/swap headroom, keeps compute-bound workers productive on non-heavy idle backlog, syncs the Cold-Start Handover Runbook to the shared beans branch on every tick so any cold successor can take over in under 60 seconds, and publishes the anti-shorthand two-table status report according to the user's selected cadence."
msgstr ""

